diff --git a/doc/openocd.texi b/doc/openocd.texi
index a4ffafa..a9f5721 100644
--- a/doc/openocd.texi
+++ b/doc/openocd.texi
@@ -2717,6 +2717,53 @@ See @url{https://arm-software.github.io/CMSIS_5/DAP/html/group__DAP__Commands__g
 A dummy software-only driver for debugging.
 @end deffn
 
+@deffn {Interface Driver} {hostio4}
+Drives the nanoSoC HOSTIO4/ADP ASCII debug monitor, an AHB master reached over
+a plain byte stream (a UART character device, a pty, a unix socket, or a TCP
+endpoint).  The monitor is not a CoreSight DAP, so, like the @code{dmem}
+driver, this one emulates a MEM-AP in software and presents it over the
+@code{dapdirect_swd} transport.  The monitor's AHB decoder has no PPB region,
+so the target is normally @code{mem_ap} rather than @code{cortex_m}.
+
+@deffn {Config Command} {hostio4_port} path|host:port
+The byte stream carrying the monitor.  Required.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Config Command} {hostio4_base} offset
+Address offset added to TAR before it goes on the wire.  Default 0.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Command} {hostio4_blocksize} n
+Maximum number of words coalesced into a single @code{R<count>} block read.
+Default 16.  This is the difference between one round trip per word and one
+round trip per block.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Command} {hostio4_timeout} ms
+Per-command reply timeout.  Default 500.  After three consecutive silent
+commands the link is declared dead rather than hung.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Command} {hostio4_block_write} on|off
+Use the monitor's @code{U} block upload for multi-word writes.  Default off:
+a short @code{U} payload parks the monitor with no recovery but a reset.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Command} {hostio4_ppb_base} ap base
+Alias accesses to @code{0xE0xxxxxx} onto the top byte of @var{base} for the
+given AP, mirroring what @code{nanosoc_dbg_ahb_bridge} does in hardware.
+Disabled by default; set @var{base} to 0 to disable.
+@end deffn
+
+@deffn {Command} {hostio4_info}
+Print the configuration and the wire statistics.
+@end deffn
+
+Accesses to @code{0x2E000000-0x2FFFFFFF}, the die-to-die window, are refused
+by the driver: the monitor has no bus timeout, so an access there while the
+die-to-die link is down stalls the AHB until the chip is reset.
+@end deffn
+
 @deffn {Interface Driver} {ep93xx}
 Cirrus Logic EP93xx based single-board computer bit-banging (in development)
 @end deffn
